{
  "summary": "Validates the announced coin count in UTXO snapshot metadata against the unique UTXO count after import, and rejects transaction groups containing zero coins. This prevents snapshot files with duplicate coin records from passing validation with inflated coin counts and closes a loop interrupt bypass from empty groups.",
  "problem": "Snapshot loading does not verify that the announced coin count in snapshot metadata matches the unique UTXOs actually imported. Duplicated outpoint records collapse into single entries in the UTXO set and match the committed UTXO hash, leaving `loadtxoutset` to report an inflated `coins_loaded` count. Additionally, empty transaction groups (specifying zero coins) are accepted without advancing the coin counter, bypassing shutdown interrupt checks during parsing.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Repeated outpoints collapse into one coin, so a snapshot can repeat every record, announce the doubled count, and still match the committed UTXO hash. loadtxoutset then reports the inflated count as coins_loaded.'",
    "PR description: 'They leave the UTXO hash unchanged and don't advance the coin count, so parsing them bypasses the interrupt check and can delay shutdown.'"
  ],
